		<title type="html"><![CDATA[New GD77/RD5R/DM1801 Beta 2024 12 12]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4660&amp;p=34568#p34568"><![CDATA[
A new GD-77 / DM-1801 / RD-5R / GD-77S Beta is now available<br><br>See<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/GD77/Firmware/1c7bedd437e088824e081882dca55736c5e5eb0c/" class="postlink">downloads/GD77/Firmware/1c7bedd437e0888 ... 6c5e5eb0c/</a><br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/GD77/Firmware/Latest" class="postlink">downloads/GD77/Firmware/Latest</a><br><br>There are no new features in this version.<br><br>This release is mainly to synchronise the MK22 MCU codebase with the MD-UV380 codebase. <br><br>The only functionality change is change the default setting for the Display Info.  Options -&gt; Display Options -&gt; Info,  so that the TS and Power overrides are displayed.<br><br><strong class="text-strong">EDIT (f1rmb)</strong><br>There are some missing updates:<ul><li> Add ability to store current GPS position in channel's Lat/Lon.<br> - On GPS featured devices, editing the Channel details Lat or Lon, longpress the STAR key will store current GPS position (if GPS is on, and fix acquired).</li><li> Add an option to disable any channel change (on Flash).<br>- see "Locked: Off/On" in General options. When it's on, SK2 + Green don't write the changes to the flash.</li><li> Fix APRS position conversion.<br>- In some case, the conversion to minutes goes wrong, and ambiguity can make it worse.</li><li> Fix DMTF entering and more:<br> - it was impossible to enter DTMF sequences on MD-UV390/MD-2017/MD-9600.<br> - A/B/C/D was unavailable in the numerical input.<br> - Many problem while txing<br> - it was impossible on most platform to navigate the contact (DMR/DTMF), from within Channel/VFO screen (no effect from Up/Down keys).<br> - On MD-9600, While using the numerical input (DTMF), long press 'A' permits to exit that screen</li></ul><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Dec 12, 2024 8:55 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
